  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>ENG2_U04_L01_GP_Q01</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ENG2_U04_L01_GP_Q01</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.ENG2.RS.01</p><p>Topic: school gardens. Which research question has the best scope for one assignment?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>ENG2_U04_L01_GP_Q01</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>none</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Are gardens good?</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Incorrect. This is too broad and mostly opinion-based.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>How could a school garden support science learning for tenth-grade students during one semester?</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct. This question is focused by topic, audience, subject area, and time frame.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>What is a plant?</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Incorrect. This is too narrow and asks for a simple definition.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Why should everyone love gardens forever?</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Incorrect. This wording is biased and too broad.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>ENG2_U04_L01_GP_Q02</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ENG2_U04_L01_GP_Q02</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.ENG2.RS.01</p><p>A student asks, &quot;What about recycling?&quot; What is the main problem with this research question?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>ENG2_U04_L01_GP_Q02</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>none</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>It is too narrow because it can be answered with one fact.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Incorrect. The problem is not that it is too narrow.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>It is already fully refined.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Incorrect. It needs a focus, audience, place, or effect.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>It includes too much evidence.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Incorrect. It includes no evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>It is only a vague topic, not a focused research question.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct. It does not ask what the student wants to learn about recycling.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
